e to attachment of dissimilar metals? Can the engines be gimballed according to specifications? Can the engine be clustered, if necessary? Can the engine be attached to air frames other than the one presently contemplated? Has it been confirmed that all parts can be made? Has it been confirmed that there is no cheaper way of making these parts? Can the parts readily be assembled, with a minimum of special tools? Has it been made impossible to incorrectly assemble and install any part? (Or incorrectly reassemble and reinstall them in the field?) Will all parts requiring service be readily accessible, prior to and following mating of the engine with the vehicle? Have all markings been called out completely and correctly? Do instructions for inspection and quality control leave no gap? Has it been ascertained that (without penalty) the design cannot save further weight? Is the envelope the smallest possible? Can the system be drained, readily and completely? (Avoidance of traps, low spots, etc.) Have engine propellant feed system components, including pumps and thrust chamber, been designed for minimum trapped propellants after cutoff? (Minimum wet weight) Has the purchasing department been appraised of the significance of mandatory (proven) sources, where applicable? Can it be transported? In one or several pieces?
• Availability and application of an effective failure
analysis and correction system.
• Last, but not least, the experience, knowledge,
analytical capabilities and judgment of the
designer himself.
