Evaluation of failure modes. There are three
basic types of failure mode: elastic deflection,
permanent plastic deformation, and fracture.
Although not a material failure, elastic deflection
may cause a part to perform improperly, resulting in
malfunction of a component or system. The other
two—plastic deformation and fracture—are material
failures influenced by material properties, load and
