The propellant combination of liquid oxygen
(LOX) and kerosene-type RP-1 fuel was selected for
the A-l engine, principally because high perfor
mance will not be as critical for booster first stages as
for upper stages. Moreover, both propellants are
abundantly available and comparatively inexpensive;
the fluids and their combustion products are
"docile"; their corrosivity is nil. Both fluids are rela
