ters. The engine schematic diagram appears in Fig. 3
3. Note that engine parameters are based on vacuum
conditions—because A-2 starts and operates in a
vacuum for its entire duration. In the case of the A-2
Stage, the starting altitude of 250,000 ft can be
considered absolute vacuum, for all practical pur
poseGs.imballing the entire engine applies TVC. The
engine weighs approximately 2181 Ib dry, 2317 Ib wet,
and 2292 Ib at burnout. The overall dimensions and
the preliminary design layout of the A-2 engine are
