Cutoff Sequence
The cutoff signal, received from the vehicle
programmer, de-energizes the engine-control valve
causing it to close. This closure vents the open side
and pressurizes the closing side of the main propel
lant-valve actuators. By proper orificing of the he
lium lines, the main oxidizer valve is made to close
faster than the main fuel valve, to ensure a fuel-rich
cutoff. The valve closure causes engine thrust to de
cay. The fuel bleed valve opens after venting of the
helium pressure in its actuator.
